  - "\u307E\u3060\u30AF\u30FC\u30EB\u30C0\u30A6\u30F3\u4E2D\u3060\u3088"
  en:
  - With 25% and a higher ticket budget enabled, idle mode can buy tickets without
    asking each time, spending up to 25% of your available balance per purchase,
    and keep opening with your current settings. You can switch to a lower budget
    or use the higher ticket budget.
  - <size=65%><color=#B8C7B8>Total opened</color></size>  <b>{0}</b> <size=60%>tickets</size>
  - 'Buy Idle. In VR, pull the lever down to start, up to stop.

    On PC, click
    the lever. Picking up tickets stops Idle.

    Reveal 10 purchased tickets to
    also use Open all.'
  - '<b>Ricorine</b>

    The mysterious cat usually appears only in friends'' photos.
    Today she is at the door. You wonder if you imagined it; she wonders if you have
    looked enough.'
  - '<b>Mamehinata</b>

    The meetup has not started, but the floor is already
    her racetrack. Everyone is looking for her; she is partying by their feet.'
  - '<b>Usasaki</b>

    She came to listen, then claimed the best mirror spot. Asked
    what she is doing, she answers very loudly with silence.'
  - '<b>Kuon</b>

    The cat is waiting by the mirror for someone to offer a headpat.
    She does not need one; she just happens to be sitting conveniently.'
  - '<b>Suzuhana</b>

    A rare guest has a special entrance: every conversation
    stops at once. She is still outside, but a place is ready.'
  - '<b>CarukiaRe</b>

    Everyone calls the cat aloof, and she agrees. Then she
    quietly moves within headpat range, still very aloof.'
  - '<b>Kipfel</b>

    The baguette is ready. Lunch or melee weapon? One thing is
    certain: the mirror corner will not be quiet today.'
  - '<b>Kokoa</b>

    The mysterious friend is finally online, but has not joined.
    Everyone acts casual while checking the doorway for the eight-hundredth time.'
  - '<b>Minahoshi</b>

    The headpat queue reaches outside before she even joins.
    Can pretending to sleep skip the introductions?'
  - '<b>Koyuki</b>

    Just one more outfit edit before bed. Third night running,
    and there is still one last color to try in the mirror.'
  - '<b>Photica</b>

    The cat announces she is tonight''s star. The photo has
    not begun; never mind, she will reserve the center now.'
  - '<b>Maya</b>

    A friend says they will be right back after changing outfits.
    Maya has arranged the photo; ten minutes later, perhaps they are changing the
    whole wardrobe.'
  - '<b>MerryMare</b>

    Her plan is flawless: pass you, pretend not to notice,
    pass you again. She is now on lap four.'
  - The tiny sad violin starts before the hamster knows what happened. Seeing you
    hold a ticket was enough to prepare for emotional damage.
  - The orbs are spinning; the Claw committee is meeting. The calculator wants value.
    The heart says Claw is law.
  - 'Challenge: last to leave the ticket wins the prize. MrBeast has the camera ready;
    reveal the arena.'
  - The happy tune is playing nearby, but Banana Cat is ready to cry for every ticket
    that lost before seeing this one.
  - Rusk declares the mirror corner closed, then sits down first. Staff must check
    the seats for comfort.
  - 'The stream is heating up, and Speed has not seen the result. Be ready: celebrations
    are rarely gentle on the microphone.'
  - '<b>Moe</b>

    Just browsing, no new outfits. Moe in the mirror agrees; Moe
    in the shopping cart has no comment.'
  - Pop Cat has clicked countless times. It can chase the world rankings, but you
    must reveal this ticket yourself.
  - '<b>Airi</b>

    Airi says no photos today. The moment a friend lifts a camera,
    she has found the best lighting.'
  - Nobody has seen this outfit. Lime enters and meets three friends wearing the
    same one. Now who gets the middle?
  - Chiffon wants a quiet moment. A passing headpat persuades her to extend that
    moment until sunrise.
  - The group photo needs just one more guest. Chocolat hears them and saves her
    entrance for the perfect moment.
  - Others debate which ticket is luckiest. He simply nods, so calm that the entire
    argument runs out of words.
  - Are you OK? Now you can answer happily. The rare guest arrives, and this launch
    delivers luck directly to you.
  - Karin will sleep early tonight. Someone starts a song; first she must identify
    it, then identify the next one.
  - The result is hidden, but the eyebrow is already raised. An imaginary bass thud
    makes even the ticket look suspicious.
  - Some cats walk on paws; this one crosses space like an endless progress bar.
    You can almost hear the loop before the rainbow arrives.
  - The launch has not started, but the audience is ready for the famous greeting.
    You check the ticket; he wants to know how you are doing.
  - A safe run, he said, before trading health for damage again. If it dies first,
    there is no need to block.
  - Others check prices at the shop. He checks whether the entrance has enough ceremony.
    The throne can follow; the presence must arrive first.
  - She says stay calm, then considers taking everything next turn. A friend says
    calculate first; she nods without leaving the prize window.
  - "Blue starter: guaranteed 100, even unopened \u2192 Buy \u2192 Hold 0.6s \u2192
    Insert winners to collect"
  - A friend says Mint looks familiar. Maybe yesterday? In fact, yesterday, the day
    before, and last week were all spent at the same mirror.
  - The crafting table is ready; Steve needs materials. Others mine diamonds. Could
    this ticket craft a little luck instead?
  - The little pets are queuing; the big dog speaks for all of them. You can almost
    hear it demanding a look at this ticket.
  - She says she will act in a moment, while her companion moves ahead. Taking turns
    at work? Neither intends to slack off.
  - Plum came for a quick mirror break and got pulled into a photo. One picture,
    then log off.
  - Your reveal was quick. The master keeps the explanation short, leaving you the
    luck and a familiar parting warning.
  - You reveal the ticket, and the loud reaction turns into a celebration. Still
    loud, now cheering for you.
  - He vows never to pull another ticket. A firm declaration, until he passes the
    box and sneaks a look at the prize window.
  - You found the cat and caught the bread attack. Today's loot is a ticket worth
    keeping, not crumbs.
  - The final guest arrived right beside you. Before the family photo is complete,
    your collection has its finale.
  - You opened the ticket and finished the challenge. The prize is no clickbait headline,
    just your lucky find.
  - Two and a half years of practice, one ticket pull from the stage. The performance
    and basketball are ready; all it needs is a cue.
  - No more lethal calculations for this ticket. You keep the result; he saves the
    remaining luck for the next campfire.
  - "PC: \u2190 / \u2192 to select; hold left mouse to reveal.\nVR: left / right
    grip to select; hold the trigger to reveal."
  - The wait is over, and you arrived. Maya saved the middle of the photo; a collection
    can be a portrait too.
  - 'Inspection complete: your collection spot is comfortable too. Rusk approves
    reopening and stays for the trial.'
  - He is already jumping. While you check the prize, he celebrates this ticket like
    a last-minute winner.
  - It is good news. The hamster freezes, the imaginary violin misses its cue, and
    you keep the lucky moment.
  - You are the audience now. Luck makes a neat turn and lands straight in your collection.
  - Shivs, poison, or one more draw? Her turn looks quiet; the hand behind it is
    already a small army.
  - The quiet spectator now has a place in your collection. No acceptance speech,
    just a spot saved for you.
  - You pulled her out of the one-last-edit loop. Tonight can finally end; this ticket
    needs no recoloring.
  - 'This is more than an online notification: she arrived. Stop watching the door;
    the rare guest is in your collection.'
  - 'No illusion: the mysterious cat chose you. A tiny photo cameo became a very
    special place in your collection.'
  - The playlist is still going, and you found her. Tonight's bonus track is called
    Good Luck Finally Arrived.
  - The rainbow reached your ticket box. The meowing may loop forever; this rare
    keepsake is no distant dot anymore.
  - The result voids the vow immediately. Looking at your winning ticket, he discovers
    it was worth it after all.
  - This draw found the character himself. Orbs and Claw call a truce, unanimously
    saving this luck for your collection.
  - You found her. Introductions can wait; the headpat queue has one more person,
    and she is staying awake for you.
  - Still aloof, now beside you. She pushes the winning ticket over and pretends
    it is no big deal.
  - The door opened, and the rare guest came for you. While everyone asks who arrived,
    you have the keepsake.
  - Crafting complete. No chicken jockey jumped out, just Steve giving your lucky
    find an approving nod.
  - No tears needed for this ticket. Banana Cat considers switching its imaginary
    soundtrack to the happy version.
  - 'One look, verdict: still unopened. The inspection panel is ready; the ticket
    refuses to give away its answer.'
  - The lightning routine is ready, but the prize window is closed. A friendly spar,
    says the master; luck wants another round.
  - This turn's good news reached you. She and her companion found their rhythm and
    delivered the keepsake together.
  - Calm became delight. No miscalculation and no restart; the rare visitor is now
    in your collection.
  - "Your tickets \xB7 {0} wrapped bundles\n{1} unrevealed \xB7 {2} winners\nUnclaimed
    winnings {3}"
  - 'You finally looked down. Her expedition is a success: straight from the ticket
    into your collection.'
  - One last picture, she says, and gives you another keepsake. Photos turn pages;
    this lucky moment stays.
  - You finally opened the ticket. The plan is complete; delivering luck to you was
    merely a happy coincidence.
  - That familiar face is now your keepsake. This meeting was not a coincidence;
    luck stopped just for you.
  - You show him the result, and the eyebrow approves. That thud is your entrance
    sound now.
  - Pop! This click finally found some luck. The counter continues, with this one
    saved in your collection.
  - This time you drew her first. The final card is revealed, and luck stays in your
    collection instead of the discard pile.
  - Your luck landed beside her. She will not admit she was waiting, but your collection
    spot is ready.
  - Waiting became a keepsake. She is not asking you to leave; this collection spot
    can stay warm a little longer.
  - You reveal the ticket and provide the final cheer. The throne is his; the keepsake
    of this win is yours.
  - 'Reveal and redeem the blue starter for 100$.

    Then take tickets or packs
    from the belt; pay on pickup.'
  - No outfit checkout this time. You found her, and she brought this good luck straight
    into your collection.
  - This ticket captured the star. With a nod, she approves adding your lucky moment
    to her personal exhibition.
  - The photo is not finished, but you already found her. Logging off can wait for
    a little celebration.
  - You found your own Lime. Outfits may match, but this lucky ticket has chosen
    you.
  - You found that quiet confidence. He nods, you nod; this lucky moment needs no
    debate.
  - 'One look, verdict: a real win. No zooming for clues; the result is right in
    your hand.'
